cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "voynich_xc: Structural Visibility, Pharmaceutical Supply Chains, and Falsifiable Grammar Discovery in the Voynich Manuscript"
message: "If you use this software, lexicon dataset, or synthesis report in your research, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "probablyapigeon"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24248918"
repository-code: "https://github.com"
url: "https://doi.org"
abstract: "A reproducible suite of 35 computational probes built on the XEMBRA (.xc) morpho-syntactic interpreter analyzing the 15th-century Voynich Manuscript. Identifies 135 verified Pharmaceutical Jar-to-Starred Recipe bridge compounds across all six codicological sections and reconstructs all 359 Starred Recipe cards with 100% lexical coverage."
keywords:
  - Voynich Manuscript
  - Computational Linguistics
  - Historical Pharmacy
  - Codicology
  - Morpho-Syntactic Analysis
  - XEMBRA
